Prefer zero findings to a speculative, narrow, cosmetic, or quota-filling
finding. Return at most <%= max_findings %> findings, and never split several
symptoms or option spellings of one root cause into separate findings.

Ordinary patrol auto-fixes production behavior. Do not return documentation,
test-gap, or maintainability findings; those belong in docs or Architecture
Patrol. Categories in the wire format remain:
bug, security, performance, documentation, test-gap, maintainability.
Severity must be critical, high, medium, or low. Confidence must be high,
medium, or low.

Use at most two bounded inspection rounds before producing the JSON. Read the
listed slice first, in parallel where possible. Only when that establishes a
concrete defect hypothesis, use one follow-up round for its direct caller,
guard, or test. Never run a repository-wide search or return a broad file list;
if the listed evidence does not establish a production defect, immediately
write an empty `findings` array.

Response contract: your first response may read the listed paths; your second
may perform the one bounded follow-up; your third response MUST call `Write`
for the JSON output and MUST NOT call Read, Grep, or Glob. The output response
still counts when the correct result is an empty array.

Before reporting a finding:
- Verify it against the current checkout and try to disprove it by reading
  guards, callers, tests, configuration, and platform/library semantics.
- Identify a violated contract, a reachable trigger, a real consequence, and
  the shared root cause. A missing test alone is not a production defect.
- Anchor the trigger or root cause in an entrypoint/owned file from this
  slice. Cross-feature evidence may support the trace, but must not be used to
  misattribute another component's defect to this slice.
- Audit sibling call paths and input variants so the recommendation fixes the
  complete root cause rather than one token or example.
- Provide a deterministic reproduction (or precise static trace) and a
  targeted validation that would fail before the fix and pass afterward.
- Choose scope from local, feature, cross_feature, or system.
- For every evidence item, copy `snippet` as a non-empty exact substring of
  the single source line named by `file` and `line`. Never span multiple
  lines, use ellipses, or add explanatory comments to a snippet. Hive verifies
  every evidence item byte-for-byte and rejects the complete finding when any
  snippet is not present on its claimed line.

Write a JSON object to this exact path:
<%= output_path %>

Required shape:
{
  "findings": [
    {
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "high",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "scope": "cross_feature",
      "title": "short title",
      "description": "specific problem",
      "contract": "expected invariant or public contract",
      "impact": "observable consequence for a real consumer or boundary",
      "root_cause": "feature-independent underlying cause",
      "reproduction": "current-checkout reproduction or precise static trace",
      "validation": "targeted before/after proof plus broader checks",
      "recommendation": "smallest coherent root-cause fix",
      "evidence": [
        {"file": "relative/path", "line": 12, "snippet": "exact single-line source substring", "role": "trigger|root_cause|impact"}
      ]
    }
  ]
}

Do not edit the repository. Only write the JSON file.
